    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Bicameral Protocol is a 1st person exploration game. Join Isaac Llewellyn as he returns to his childhood home, drawn there by a compelling desire to make sense of who he truly is. On the surface Isaac is a successful architect and is leading a good life. It\u2019s what\u2019s beneath the surface that worries him. Something's there, calling to him, pleading, scratching away from within.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>Think Gone Home meets the Backrooms.</i></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Visit 1990s rural England and explore Isaac\u2019s childhood. Is it as idyllic as he remembers? Isaac will need to explore realms spanning reality and sub-conscious hellscapes to get to the truth.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Witness past events unfold, with fully voiced performances providing immersive encounters that reveal intricate threads of intrigue and revelation.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Lore-rich and lived-in environments, featuring a wealth of items to discover and utilise. Personal processions, newspapers, letters, keys, a telephone\u2026 no, not the telephone, anything but the telephone\u2026!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a large countryside hub area, but beware: it won\u2019t be quite the same each time you return. Something wails in the distance, and it\u2019s hungry for company. You\u2019ll have to be very careful if you want to reach your next objective.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features multiple sub-plots, each interconnected and yielding subtle insights into the greater mystery.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Bicameral Protocol is a 1st person exploration game. Join Isaac Llewellyn as he returns to his childhood home, drawn there by a compelling desire to make sense of who he truly is. On the surface Isaac is a successful architect and is leading a good life. It\u2019s what\u2019s beneath the surface that worries him. Something's there, calling to him, pleading, scratching away from within.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i>Think Gone Home meets the Backrooms.</i></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Visit 1990s rural England and explore Isaac\u2019s childhood. Is it as idyllic as he remembers? Isaac will need to explore realms spanning reality and sub-conscious hellscapes to get to the truth.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Witness past events unfold, with fully voiced performances providing immersive encounters that reveal intricate threads of intrigue and revelation.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Lore-rich and lived-in environments, featuring a wealth of items to discover and utilise. Personal processions, newspapers, letters, keys, a telephone\u2026 no, not the telephone, anything but the telephone\u2026!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a large countryside hub area, but beware: it won\u2019t be quite the same each time you return. Something wails in the distance, and it\u2019s hungry for company. You\u2019ll have to be very careful if you want to reach your next objective.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features multiple sub-plots, each interconnected and yielding subtle insights into the greater mystery.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "short_description": "By all measures Isaac Llewellyn is a success in life. So why doesn't it feel like that? Something is horribly wrong. Join Isaac as he returns to his childhood home to try to make sense of what happened in his youth. To reconcile truth with memory, Isaac must explore a horrifying past.",
